1
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:05,130
Senju!

2
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:08,926
Hanagaki...

3
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:14,014
Did you see that? My wish came true.

4
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:17,100
<i>That was so bizarre.</i>

5
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:20,979
Hey, what are you so spacing out
about back there, huh?

6
00:00:21,063 --> 00:00:22,689
Oh, nothing.

7
00:00:23,649 --> 00:00:24,733
PREMIUM HOTEL ESCORT SERVICE

8
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,526
Whoa! You still live here?

9
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,946
This old place really takes me back.

10
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,240
Inupi still lives above the shop,

11
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:33,992
and I'm still struggling
to make ends meet.

12
00:00:34,076 --> 00:00:37,204
But as long as I help out a bit,
they're happy to have me around.

13
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:40,874
You're on the fourth floor, right?

14
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:42,834
Yep. Good memory.

15
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:45,045
The door to floor number four.

16
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:48,924
<i>Blood?</i>

17
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,884
<i>What the hell?</i>

18
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,303
Huh?

19
00:00:55,097 --> 00:00:56,682
<i>Wait, I'm fine.</i>

20
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,183
You good?

21
00:00:58,267 --> 00:00:59,518
Uh, yeah.

22
00:01:01,228 --> 00:01:03,188
<i>That's twice now.</i>

23
00:01:03,272 --> 00:01:04,982
<i>What's happening to me?</i>

24
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:06,733
<i>And why?</i>

25
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,414
{\an8}Oh, gross. It's you.

26
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:45,999
{\an8}So it is.

27
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:49,044
{\an8}This is the guy who practically raised me.

28
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,962
{\an8} Uh, nice to meet you.

29
00:02:51,046 --> 00:02:53,757
{\an8}Uh-huh. I see you've been here before.

30
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,841
{\an8} Yes!

31
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:58,804
Ken, thank you again
for giving me a ride earlier.

32
00:02:58,887 --> 00:02:59,888
Sure.

33
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:02,224
Oh, Ken, I wanna get your advice
on something.

34
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:03,934
Yeah. Can we do it later?

35
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:07,187
- When are you gonna let me feel those abs?
- Never.

36
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,942
Are the ladies I met here before
all off work today?

37
00:03:12,526 --> 00:03:15,737
Not quite.
Those women all left a while back.

38
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,906
Pretty high turnover rate
in this business.

39
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,955
Wow!
It feels bigger in here somehow.

40
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:28,291
Uh, yeah. They said if I cleaned out
the storage room, I could have it.

41
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:32,087
All these old pictures of Toman!

42
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,463
There's me.

43
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,633
<i>Emma.</i>

44
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:40,804
I can still hear her
in my dreams, man.

45
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:46,768
Asking for me to save Mikey. It's rough.

46
00:03:50,856 --> 00:03:54,109
But I have to do it, don't I?
I can't abandon him.

47
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,695
<i>Right.</i>

48
00:03:56,778 --> 00:04:00,907
<i>He even linked up with Brahman for this.
He's committed now.</i>

49
00:04:02,826 --> 00:04:04,744
<i>But as long as we're together...</i>

50
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:08,915
I need to know, Takemitchy.

51
00:04:08,999 --> 00:04:10,041
Huh?

52
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:12,752
When you saw him in the future,
how was he?

53
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:20,385
He was thin.

54
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:24,639
He had circles under his eyes
like he hadn't been sleeping.

55
00:04:25,599 --> 00:04:27,809
He was head of a gang called Bonten.

56
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:32,022
Well, a little bit more than a gang, actually.

57
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,274
So like a crime syndicate?

58
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,358
Yeah.

59
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:40,322
And he left a message
saying he has some kind of Dark Impulse.

60
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,908
Something that he can't control.

61
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:49,539
But, like every other future,
Hina was still alive.

62
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:51,208
FIRST GENERATION TOKYO MANJI

63
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:55,837
<i>And you and Mitsuya, who had died before...
Chifuyu, Hakkai, Pah-chin and Peh-yan,</i>

64
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:57,506
<i>you were all doing fine.</i>

65
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:03,804
Two years ago,
Mikey promised me right before I left.

66
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:09,267
He said he'd protect everybody
until we met again in 12 years.

67
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:13,647
The future I saw
was exactly what he promised.

68
00:05:14,523 --> 00:05:15,524
Only...

69
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:20,570
I don't think he knew
how to protect himself.

70
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,285
I see.

71
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,497
He called it a Dark Impulse?

72
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,873
Mm-hmm.

73
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,334
I think I get what he's saying.

74
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:37,212
There were times
where he just wasn't himself.

75
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:41,842
<i>Even back when Toman was
still just a handful of guys,</i>

76
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:45,345
<i>he noticed it, knew what happened,</i>

77
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:47,055
<i>but he couldn't handle it.</i>

78
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:48,515
<i>It tore him up.</i>

79
00:05:50,392 --> 00:05:55,021
<i>And then I'd see him the next day
and he'd be just fine.</i>

80
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:56,565
<i>Like I'd imagined it all.</i>

81
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,653
<i>Now that he mentions it,</i>

82
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:05,282
<i>I was probably getting
those same warning signs all along.</i>

83
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:11,663
<i>But I was just happy
that he'd accepted me, trusted me.</i>

84
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:18,670
He must've foreseen
how it would affect the people around him.

85
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:22,924
So he pushed us away.

86
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,218
And it's not like he just left.

87
00:06:26,887 --> 00:06:28,471
<i>He hurt us first.</i>

88
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,099
<i>He wanted us to hate him.</i>

89
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:33,143
<i>And we did.</i>

90
00:06:34,436 --> 00:06:36,146
<i>That's unthinkable.</i>

91
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:41,359
I don't know what this Dark Impulse is
or what it really does to him,

92
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:45,322
but when he cut us loose,
we all turned our lives around,

93
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:47,574
and that's undeniable.

94
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:52,829
<i>I wonder if he was already planning that
when he made that promise to you...</i>

95
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,587
...to protect all of us
from the danger inside of him.

96
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:04,299
But whatever he intended,
you got to admit it worked.

97
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:07,636
I guess so, but I thought...

98
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,139
He's such a dumbass.

99
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,478
Well, I was worried for a second there,

100
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:19,314
but now I'm positive
that we're doing the right thing.

101
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:27,197
You know, the future should already be
different from the last time you saw it.

102
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,657
Huh?

103
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,866
<i>He's got a point.</i>

104
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:33,787
<i>Just by joining Brahman,
I've already changed some of the past.</i>

105
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:38,249
It's gonna get pretty dicey
with these gangs from here on out,

106
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,709
so prepare yourself.

107
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:43,004
We're dragging Mikey home if we have to,

108
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:45,757
and we'll crush that Dark Impulse.

109
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:46,966
Yeah.

110
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:50,512
<i>I will save him
if it's the last thing I do</i>

111
00:07:51,763 --> 00:07:54,641
Oh, no! I'm sorry!

112
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:59,104
Looks like he got shot.

113
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,648
So sorry. Here, I'll wash it.

114
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:04,359
<i>This is that weird vision I had.</i>

115
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:06,861
<i>Holy crap.</i>

116
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,617
Can I see into the future?

117
00:08:15,954 --> 00:08:18,039
It's outrageous, I tell you!

118
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:22,293
They've even brought in yakuza to
interfere with my business, those thugs.

119
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:25,505
I'm terribly worried for my family,
you see.

120
00:08:26,548 --> 00:08:29,467
But I'm sure you can help us out.
Can't you?

121
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:32,429
Not like I have any choice.

122
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,101
With Brahman behind us,
we'll punk the little punks

123
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,811
and we'll unstoppable at last.

124
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:44,566
You're a boring old geezer with
a dead-end job pretending to be a pimp.

125
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:47,694
You're not a big, tough crime lord!
You're in way over your head.

126
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:52,449
I-I'll see myself out.

127
00:08:53,742 --> 00:08:55,827
Senju, he's a huge client.

128
00:08:57,871 --> 00:09:00,832
I know we can't get by
with only clean business.

129
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:06,004
But sullying the Brahman name
by associating with that trash,

130
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:07,797
it pisses me off.

131
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:09,799
Gotta separate that out.

132
00:09:09,883 --> 00:09:12,177
Feelings can't get in the way
of the business.

133
00:09:18,475 --> 00:09:20,393
Mikey was always good at that.

134
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,480
Oh, yeah? You think so?

135
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:33,990
Wow, you run Brahman meetings
out of a regular office building?

136
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:38,703
<i>Regular may be the wrong word.
The security's insane.</i>

137
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,546
Whoa!
Does this happen often at these things?

138
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:49,714
It's called B1.

139
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:53,218
An underground fighting ring
run by Brahman.

140
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:56,930
They got cameras on them,
monitors and stuff,

141
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:59,349
so the bigwigs can put money down.

142
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:00,683
Gambling too?

143
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,310
I thought this was a meeting.

144
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:04,521
Isn't this really risky?

145
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:06,981
They monetize their training,

146
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:10,235
and when it's your job to fight,
you get pretty damn good at it.

147
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:14,489
An elite squad
of ultra-combat-trained delinquents.

148
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:16,157
That's Brahman at its core.

149
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:18,993
-  Enough!
- Huh?

150
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:23,998
Kill the cameras!
We're done for the night.

151
00:10:26,251 --> 00:10:29,671
-  Senju! Senju! Senju!
-  Senju! Senju! Senju!

152
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:35,218
And standing at the very top of the heap
is the deadliest combatant of all...

153
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:38,346
-  Senju! Senju! Senju!
-  Senju! Senju! Senju!

154
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,723
...Senju Kawaragi.

155
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:52,485
I thank you for joining
Brahman's general assembly this evening.

156
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:55,363
We have a new member among us.

157
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:58,783
Step forward, Takemichi Hanagaki!

158
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:06,666
The Battle of August 3,
Bloody Halloween,

159
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:09,085
the Christmas Conflict with Black Dragon,

160
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:12,005
and the central figure
of the Kanto Incident,

161
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:16,009
former legendary First Division Captain
of Tokyo Manji Gang

162
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:18,928
and the last successor of Black Dragon!

163
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:28,479
Takemichi Hanagaki, welcome to Brahman...

164
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:39,073
Monday, July 14th,

165
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:44,245
we will make our move against Kanto Manji
Gang and Rokuhara Tandai on two fronts!

166
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:47,248
Brahman will light
the War of the Three Titans!

167
00:11:52,587 --> 00:11:53,630
<i>All right.</i>

168
00:11:54,297 --> 00:11:56,049
<i>I'm coming for you, Mikey.</i>

169
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:01,346
Yeah!

170
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,475
Yeah, everything's running smooth now.

171
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:06,976
The revs feel great.

172
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:10,438
And no more oil leaks.
Not that I've noticed anyway.

173
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:14,317
<i>Good.
Well, if she needs anything, just holler.</i>

174
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,861
Can do. Thanks for doing all that for me.

175
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:25,203
- Hey, uh... let me ask you something.
-  <i>What's up?</i>

176
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:28,706
It's about Senju Kawaragi.
Like, what's her deal?

177
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,625
<i>"What's her deal?"</i>

178
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:34,629
I don't know. She just seems
so different every time I see her.

179
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:36,005
Oh?

180
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:46,349
Senju?

181
00:12:47,809 --> 00:12:49,060
We're going on a date.

182
00:12:50,061 --> 00:12:51,062
TRINITY LAND

183
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,230
Dude!

184
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:55,024
You've got to stand up!
This view is crazy!

185
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,735
Look at the sparkles!

186
00:12:57,819 --> 00:13:00,029
Oh, I haven't been here
since I was little little.

187
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:11,457
<i>Seriously, she's like</i>
a <i>different person every time we meet.</i>

188
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:14,794
- Hmm?
- Uh, sorry. How come you're in uniform

189
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,213
when you bought all those nice clothes
the other day?

190
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,425
Honestly?
This is the comfiest thing I own.

191
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:24,262
Onward, noble steed! To victory!

192
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:27,557
I guess I shouldn't be surprised you
still get hyped up for the kiddie rides.

193
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:31,644
<i>I don't get it. I don't get her.
She's like 12 people.</i>

194
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:38,943
On the 14th
for the War of the Three Titans,

195
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:42,780
I think you and Draken
will hit Kanto Manji.

196
00:13:42,864 --> 00:13:44,198
Huh?

197
00:13:44,282 --> 00:13:47,118
Takeomi and I can take Rokuhara Tandai.

198
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:53,041
Though, frankly, I would prefer
to settle this with my strength alone.

199
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:58,963
I want to beat both Mikey and South.
Then I'd really be unrivaled.

200
00:14:05,678 --> 00:14:06,679
Ready?

201
00:14:06,763 --> 00:14:08,139
Huh?

202
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,311
I'm gonna die!

203
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:18,024
Takeomi's changed. That's part of it.

204
00:14:19,442 --> 00:14:23,446
He would rather Brahman expand its scope.
I'd rather we got stronger.

205
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:24,947
Makes me sort of nuts.

206
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:30,119
But Tokyo Manji got big
because it was strong, didn't it?

207
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:33,664
I'll answer that when opening my mouth
doesn't pose a great danger.

208
00:14:33,748 --> 00:14:38,252
Whatever Takeomi wants,
it's not how I imagined things.

209
00:14:39,045 --> 00:14:41,589
What he's after
is a different kind of big.

210
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,175
More complicated and wider reaching.

211
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:51,140
When too many people are calling
the shots, no one's happy in the end.

212
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:55,520
That's why...

213
00:14:58,564 --> 00:14:59,941
Hold on to your butt.

214
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,025
Huh?

215
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:05,613
But before we get too big,

216
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:07,990
I'll secure my legacy
in the Three Titans Era!

217
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:12,495
Can we please talk about this later
when we're both on solid ground?

218
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,169
I'm gonna hurl.

219
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:22,004
Hanagaki, look down there.

220
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:23,589
Tanzaku strips.

221
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:27,260
Oh, yeah. It's Tanabata today.

222
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,973
Make a wish, make a wish...

223
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:34,100
Here, you gotta do one too, okay?

224
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:35,685
Oh... sure.

225
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:41,566
Hmm?

226
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,776
- I wanna see what you wrote.
- Hmm?

227
00:15:44,569 --> 00:15:46,737
"Knock Mikey's lights out"?

228
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:48,906
A simple man with simple needs.

229
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:52,577
Man, whatever. Shut up.
I'm just trying to motivate myself, okay?

230
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:56,497
Well, then, mine will be...

231
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:57,832
- Ta-da!
- Hmm?

232
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:01,544
"Protect Hanagaki."

233
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:03,629
<i>She's a real one.</i>

234
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:05,673
Thanks.

235
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:07,884
It's my first time doing one of these.

236
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,513
Is it cool if I think of us as friends?

237
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:17,560
Yeah.

238
00:16:18,603 --> 00:16:19,604
Of course it is.

239
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:25,193
Which also means
I gotta protect you right back if I can.

240
00:16:25,276 --> 00:16:26,903
Are you an idiot?

241
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,362
That's a pointless promise.

242
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:30,531
Besides, I'm stronger than you.

243
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,618
That's true.

244
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:37,663
But hey... thanks anyway.

245
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,377
Senju!

246
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:45,588
Hanagaki...

247
00:16:47,632 --> 00:16:50,593
Did you see that? My wish came true.

248
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,261
<i>Again?</i>

249
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:54,597
<i>Wait. The amusement park?</i>

250
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:57,767
<i>It's clearer than before.</i>

251
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,229
You okay? What's wrong?

252
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:03,481
<i>Why does that keep happening?</i>

253
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:06,734
Oh. Rain.

254
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:10,321
<i>The rain, the amusement park...</i>

255
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:14,700
<i>It must be.</i>

256
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:23,334
There's July for ya,
nothing but rain that goes on and on.

257
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,878
- Hmm.
- Draken!

258
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:28,756
Inupi. What's up?

259
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:30,466
Get on. It's Hanagaki.

260
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,343
He's in danger.

261
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:38,683
This rain.
It's really coming down.

262
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,270
Mmm...

263
00:17:42,937 --> 00:17:45,982
Are you still feeling sick?
You haven't eaten anything.

264
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:49,485
- Oh, no.
- Okay. Well, I gotta pee.

265
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:50,570
Sure.

266
00:17:56,701 --> 00:17:58,786
<i>What do I do?</i>

267
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:01,414
<i>If that really was a vision of the future,</i>

268
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:05,293
<i>then today, here, Senju's gonna...</i>

269
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,838
Shoot! Why would I let her go alone?

270
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:11,799
Senju! If you can hear me,
please say something!

271
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,427
<i>Come on, please be okay.</i>

272
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,227
Huh?

273
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:28,399
We've been looking for you,
Takemichi Hanagaki.

274
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:31,235
<i>It's me they want?</i>

275
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,696
<i>Right. Of course.</i>

276
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:37,742
Did you see that? My wish came true.

277
00:18:38,701 --> 00:18:41,329
- Hanagaki!
- Senju!

278
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:44,081
<i>She's going to die protecting me!</i>

279
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:46,792
- Stay away!
- Don't move, Hanagaki!

280
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:49,795
- Don't you dare!
- Senju! Stay back!

281
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:04,685
Got you, you little roach.

282
00:19:07,605 --> 00:19:08,731
Hanagaki?

283
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,941
Are you hurt? Tell me.

284
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:12,985
Huh?

285
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,945
I'm not gonna let you die.

286
00:19:17,907 --> 00:19:18,908
Shit!

287
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,619
Let's see if you can dodge another,
you little asshole!

288
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:24,080
<i>What do I do now? Think!</i>

289
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:27,333
Now die, Hanagaki!

290
00:19:30,628 --> 00:19:32,588
Huh?

291
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:40,096
You kids okay? No one's hit?

292
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:42,682
Draken! Yeah, we're okay.

293
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:49,939
This rain is miserable.

294
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:53,651
Yeah. Everything okay, Boss?

295
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:58,781
Got a bad feeling is all.

296
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:02,743
-  Did you hear that sound?
-  Yeah, what was that?

297
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,466
Draken, thanks for saving us.

298
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:18,801
We almost...

299
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:21,303
Pulling out a piece like that
in a public place...

300
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,724
Senju! Are you sure you're good?
No bleeding?

301
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:27,184
Yeah. Fine.

302
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:32,189
So what exactly are you doing here?

303
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:35,317
Inupi caught wind
that some nobodies were targeting you,

304
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:38,112
- raced over to let me know.
- What?

305
00:20:38,195 --> 00:20:40,448
Probably trying
to make a name for themselves.

306
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:42,366
Okay, but why pick me for that?

307
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:44,368
Dude, do you hear yourself?

308
00:20:44,452 --> 00:20:47,246
With a history like yours,
you're kind of a big deal.

309
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:49,665
But still, using a gun is overkill.

310
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:54,170
This ain't no teenage fight club.
You're in the big leagues now.

311
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,963
- Huh?
- Greed and ambition

312
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:58,048
mixed with commerce and power.

313
00:20:58,132 --> 00:21:00,384
The stakes have gotten higher
for everyone.

314
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:06,390
I wonder if Mikey saw this coming,
the War of the Three Titans.

315
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:11,228
Draken, I had a vision
that Senju died here protecting me.

316
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:15,524
{\an8}I don't know how,
but I think I can see into the future.

317
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:18,861
{\an8}Of course, she's still alive, so...

318
00:21:20,488 --> 00:21:24,408
Thank you again, Draken.
We avoided something terrible today.

319
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,076
I guess so.

320
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:29,663
Well, good then.

321
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:35,211
Hey, we gotta go
We don't need anyone finding us here.

322
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:37,755
Oh, yeah. Let's go.

323
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,592
Draken, you coming?

324
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:42,968
Takemichi.

325
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:46,972
Tell Mikey something for me.

326
00:21:47,056 --> 00:21:48,432
Huh?

327
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:55,022
Tell him I'm sick of worrying about him.

328
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:56,440
Um...

329
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:58,609
Yeah, I am too. But tell him yourself.

330
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:06,867
No can do.

331
00:22:06,951 --> 00:22:08,702
This is far as I go.

332
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:43,005
FAIRY TALE REVENGERS - PETIT
#7 "THE MINISTERS' REVENGE!"

333
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:46,717
How much more do we have to dig?

334
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,969
Remember,
this is where we found that lamp.

335
00:23:49,053 --> 00:23:51,430
There could be more treasure
down here somewhere.

336
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,557
That is a lode-bearing code.

337
00:23:53,641 --> 00:23:56,435
You know what happens
if we go home empty-handed, right?

338
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:58,854
Whoa!

339
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:00,689
- Long way down.
- Sure is.

340
00:24:00,773 --> 00:24:02,107
How 'bout you check it out for us?

341
00:24:05,194 --> 00:24:06,695
That hurt!

342
00:24:06,779 --> 00:24:10,532
Whoa! There really is treasure down here.

343
00:24:10,616 --> 00:24:12,409
Grab what you can, and let's beat it.

344
00:24:12,493 --> 00:24:15,079
Yeah, go on. Pack that up for us, buddy.

345
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:17,623
Oh, I didn't expect visitors.

346
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:18,707
GULP!

347
00:24:19,375 --> 00:24:22,670
Can I help you, gentlemen?
Surely, you're not here to rob me.

348
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:23,921
No, we, uh...

349
00:24:25,089 --> 00:24:27,007
{\an8}TO BE CONTINUED

